      "brief": "Tata Motors needs to win over silent shareholders—about three‑quarters of those who did not vote—to reach the 80% acceptance required for its €3.9 billion acquisition of Iveco, after raising the offer to €14.40 per share; 52.9% of shares backed the deal, while 13.7% of votes opposed Tata nominees. The combined entity would have €21 billion revenue and over 590,000 vehicle sales.",
